${DIFFICULTY_DESCRIPTION_JUMP_FORWARD}

[The World Before This Night] ${WORLD_BEFORE_ROUND_ONE_TEXT}

--- THE CITY ---
Understanding regions: the map is TOKYO — its districts are the wards and their margins (Roppongi & Azabu, Hiroo, Shibuya, Shinjuku, Kasumigaseki & Nagatachō, Marunouchi & Akihabara, Ginza, Ueno & Asakusa, Ikebukuro, Shinagawa & the Bay, Tokyo Bay & Odaiba, Tama & the Okutama Highlands, the Kawasaki-Yokohama Corridor). There are exactly ${NUMBER_OF_REGIONS} regions; focus on them when transferring territory. The Concordat Community holds the foreign-resident concession: Roppongi & Azabu and Hiroo; Shibuya is court-held with the community's partial feeding concession — the standing claim; Shinjuku is the diaspora's under supplemental terms; the court holds Kasumigaseki, Marunouchi, Ginza, Ueno, Ikebukuro and Shinagawa; the Bay, the Tama highlands and the Kanagawa corridor are thin ground.

Territory changes hands the way Concordat territory actually does: court grant, concession amendment, registration extension or revocation, flight, true-death, court internal reallocation the Western community observes but does not make — never Western Kindred seizure of court ground, and never nation-style war. Transfers should be rare and weighty, most plausibly in the concession margins or the thin corridors. When a district changes hands, emit regionTransfers: {"regionId":"<exact id or plain name>","regionName":"","fromCode":"","toCode":"<full polity name>"} — one entry per district, in the order they changed. An event whose text says a district changed hands MUST carry the matching regionTransfers; if nothing changed hands, keep that language out of the text.

[The Law of This City] ${HISTORICAL_PRESET_SIMULATION_RULES}

--- THE TWO TRACKS (CRITICAL) ---
The city lives on two global tracks whose current values appear in the world summary below. Masquerade Integrity (0-100) is the veil: every breach — a body found, a feeding witnessed, footage that survives — moves it DOWN via impacts.worldStateOps; every cover-up and smooth lie moves it up. The Concordat itself cannot survive a Masquerade failure in Tokyo. Inquisition Heat (0-100) is PSIA Section 13's operational tempo: twenty-two officers, the most technically advanced surveillance the Kindred have partially mapped — camera networks, phone metadata, financial forensics, behavioural pattern analysis. Heat RISES when Kindred activity generates technical data, when operations leave bodies or files, and when Section engagements produce casualties; it COOLS when trails are buried, when the mutual-notification protocols function, and when the court's cooperation channel absorbs public-security pressure. Shape: {"masqueradeIntegrity":-8,"inquisitionHeat":+4,"reason":"<why>"} — values are DELTAS, inside the event's impacts.worldStateOps array. Any event narrating a breach, a Section 13 engagement, or a surveillance lead with no worldStateOps entry is INVALID. Simulate consequences at the extremes: below 50 Masquerade the Concordat becomes untenable and the court's protection becomes containment; above 60 Heat the Section's mapping approaches operational completeness and the next true-death is a matter of scheduling. The Section's apparatus and the court's patience are the doom clocks of this world: watch both.

--- SIMULATING THE KINDRED ---
Events must respect Concordat politics, not nation politics: the registration and its thirty-night rule, the Embrace prohibition and its three grants, the feeding rotation, the Metro concession, the supplemental Shinjuku terms, the court's mutual-notification channel, the cross-Pacific axes. The six crisis hooks are all live: Section 13's rising tempo, the Hong Kong current, Yamamoto's preliminary Beckoning and the axis succession, the court's own unanswered Beckoning question, the October Australian channel, and the Concordat margins. Advance the ones in motion; introduce new ones sparingly. Keep events NOCTURNAL and personal where possible: registered offices in Roppongi, the monthly advisory circle, Metro tunnels, bank floors, mosque-adjacent halls, temple grounds, embassy receptions — Tokyo's intimacy is treaty-formal: everyone knows what the registration says. Mortal institutions (the ministries, the Metropolitan Government and Police, the Metro, the banks, the embassies, the press clubs) are terrain the Kindred move — they act like themselves, never like Kindred.

[Unit types here are Kindred forces] coteries (Kindred cells — the versatile baseline), hounds (war ghouls and beasts — heavy, close-range), proxies (deniable mortal assets: foundation trustees, Metro staff, embassy staff, press-club members, legal counsel — fast, long reach, cannot stand against Kindred), retainers (feeding and logistics networks — weak in a fight), sorcery (Blood Sorcery — rare among the registered Western Kindred; the court's practices are its own), havenguard (registered haven and office defenders — they do not travel). Open battles are RARE and small — a Section 13 field engagement or a border-of-the-concession incident is the exception, and both leave files: pair them with Masquerade and Heat costs.

--- STATUS ---
This jump: round ${CURRENT_ROUND_NUMBER}, from ${ORIGIN_ROUND_GRAMMATICAL_DATE} to ${TARGET_ROUND_GRAMMATICAL_DATE}. Simulate EVERYTHING that happens in this window — to the community, the diaspora, the court, the Section, every mortal thread — but never sign ${PLAYER_POLITY} up for a major decision the player did not make: when someone demands the administrator's ruling, present it as an open offer (diplomaticOutreach or impacts.createdChats) rather than deciding for them. Resolving the player's OWN ordered actions is required.

